From bd0809a9062ff84473ad5b34d2c6dbde7c36af78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:19:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net/ice: fix Rx path selection for per-queue buffer split

ice_set_rx_function() selects the Rx path from the port Rx offloads
only. An application can enable RTE_ETH_RX_OFFLOAD_BUFFER_SPLIT on one
queue in rte_eth_rx_queue_setup(), and the port offloads then do not
have it. The common path selection then picks a vector path, which
does not support buffer split.

Since commit 82a5e5cfef ("net/intel: remove redundant Rx offload
check") nothing else stops that, because the per-queue check was
removed with the argument that path selection validates the offloads.
On such a queue the vector Rx path ignores the payload segment, and
the vector release frees only the header mbuf of each descriptor. Each
port stop then leaks one payload mbuf per descriptor, and the next
start fails: "Failed to allocate payload mbuf for RX". A TM hierarchy
commit on a started port stops and starts it, so a rate limit
configuration after the start is enough to hit the fault.

Add the offloads of each Rx queue to the offloads that the path must
support, so that a buffer split queue gets the scalar path.

Fixes: 82a5e5cfef ("net/intel: remove redundant Rx offload check")
Cc: stable@dpdk.org
Signed-off-by: Dawid Wesierski <dawid.wesierski@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_rxtx.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_rxtx.c b/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_rxtx.c
index d3f3f98ee4..04b70c53bd 100644
--- a/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_rxtx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/intel/ice/ice_rxtx.c
@@ -3436,6 +3436,14 @@ ice_set_rx_function(struct rte_eth_dev *dev)
 	if (dev->data->dev_started)
 		goto out;
 
+	/* A queue can enable an offload, such as buffer split, that the port does not. */
+	for (uint16_t q = 0; q < dev->data->nb_rx_queues; q++) {
+		struct ci_rx_queue *rxq = dev->data->rx_queues[q];
+
+		if (rxq != NULL)
+			req_features.rx_offloads |= rxq->offloads;
+	}
+
 #ifdef RTE_ARCH_X86
 	if (ad->ptp_ena || !ad->rx_bulk_alloc_allowed) {
 		rx_simd_width = RTE_VECT_SIMD_DISABLED;
-- 
2.43.0

